      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How many m/s is 100 km/h?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "100 km/h equals exactly 27.778 m/s (100 ÷ 3.6). This is the speed of a car at the common European motorway limit, or the typical cruising speed of a fast cyclist in a time trial. In physics equations, 27.778 m/s is the value to use for any 100 km/h scenario." }
